# Committed on purpose. `update.sh` deploys with `git pull` and then builds on
# the server, and NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the client bundle at
# build time — so anything not in git is simply absent in production. That is
# why the Google button never rendered on the live /signin: `.env.local` is
# gitignored and has never existed on the server.
#
# Nothing secret belongs here. Every value below ships inside the public JS
# bundle by definition; treat this file as public. Real secrets
# (BACKEND_API_URL credentials, admin tokens) stay server-side.
#
# `.env.local` still wins locally, so your machine keeps overriding these.

# Google Identity Services web client id. Must match the backend's
# GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID or the backend rejects the token's `aud`.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=275860271813-vt4mc58083hskh030i90p2cpvnih1ito.apps.googleusercontent.com

# Sign in with Apple on the web needs a *Services ID* (com.something.web).
# Do not paste a Google client id here — a Google id makes the button render and
# then fail with `invalid_client`, which is worse than staying hidden.
#
# Apple forbids the Services ID from equalling the App ID, so web cannot reuse
# `com.uplisoft.velocityesim` verbatim. It is registered under that same primary
# App ID (team R72R8C56GK) instead, which is what makes Apple issue one shared
# `sub` per user across mobile and web — same account on both.
#
# Portal requirements for this value to work in production:
#   - Services ID enabled for Sign in with Apple
#   - Grouped under primary App ID com.uplisoft.velocityesim
#   - Domain:     esim.uplisoft.com
#   - Return URL: https://esim.uplisoft.com/signin
# The backend must also set APPLE_SERVICES_ID to this exact string, or the
# token's `aud` is rejected (see E-SIM backend/src/config/index.ts).
NEXT_PUBLIC_APPLE_SERVICES_ID=com.uplisoft.velocityesim.web

# Google Ads tag (gtag.js) + purchase-conversion event id, per the Google Ads
# "set up a Google tag" instructions. src/lib/analytics.ts falls back to these
# same live values when unset, but they're pinned here explicitly so prod
# config doesn't silently depend on a hardcoded code default.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ADS_ID=AW-11016325088
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ADS_PURCHASE_LABEL=Xf_8CIug2u0cEOCP_4Qp